=====Take a sentence as input and use a dictionary to count the frequency of each word.=====

sentence= input("Enter a sentence:")
words=sentence.split()
frequency={}

for word in words:
    if word in frequency:
        frequency[word] += 1
    else:
        frequency[word] = 1

print("Word frequency:")
print(frequency)



=====Create two sets of numbers and demonstrate union, intersection, difference, and symmetric difference operations.=====

san1={10,20,25,15,44}
san2={30,50,20,44,10}
print("Union:", san1 | san2)
print("Intersection:", san1 & san2)
print("Difference:", san1 - san2)
print("Symmetric Difference:", san1 ^ san2)



